  bl.1 fountain pen|Base.Pen|His own retirement present, chosen without anyone else's advice.
  bl.2 letter notebook|Base.Notebook|Drafts outnumber addresses; some begin by correcting the reader.
  bl.3 fine-toothed comb|Base.Comb|Madeline disliked seeing his part wander across his head.
  bl.4 rain-swollen paperback||A comic novel; its first line can still make him laugh aloud.
  bl.5 enamel derby badge||Won in 1981; a fish rather than a piano made him briefly famous locally.
  bl.6 Francis's last envelope||The letter has been read many times but never answered.
  rl.1 Madeline Bishop|mother, died 1974|Born 1884; Everett cared for her in 1968-74 and postponed a promised outing.
  rl.2 Francis Bishop|older brother, died 1988|Born 1913; disagreement about Madeline's care ended their correspondence.
  rl.3 Doris Wiles|dance teacher, former employer|He accompanied her classes, then secretly learned tap from her in 1961-67.
  rl.4 Beatrice Holm and Lewis Pike|former piano pupils|Aged forty-nine and fifty-two in 1993; left at a crossing after Everett offered to escort them.
end

